    "content": "The National Independent Electoral and Boundaries Commission (NIEBC) has announced the specific districts in Hirshabeelle State where indirect elections for the state's local council and House of Representatives will be conducted. The announcement, made on August 27, 2026, clarifies the electoral map for the upcoming polls, which will involve delegates voting in six districts in Hiiraan and six in Middle Shabelle.\n\nIn Hiiraan, the elections will take place in Beledweyne, Jalalaqsi, Buuloburde, Matabaan, Jawiil, and Farlibaax. In Middle Shabelle, the designated districts are Jowhar, Balcad, Warsheekh, Cadale, Mahaday, and one additional district yet to be confirmed. These locations were selected based on the NIEBC's mandate to oversee the electoral process in accordance with federal and state electoral laws.\n\nThe decision follows a period of preparatory work by the NIEBC, which has been coordinating with state authorities to ensure the indirect elections are held in a transparent and orderly manner. The commission's role in announcing the districts is seen as a step toward finalizing the electoral calendar for Hirshabeelle, which is part of Somalia's broader push toward universal suffrage, though indirect voting remains in place for this cycle.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, especially those with ties to Hirshabeelle, these elections represent a critical opportunity to influence the political landscape from abroad, as diaspora engagement can shape the outcomes through advocacy and financial support to candidates. The stability of the electoral process in Hirshabeelle is also vital for the region's development and for maintaining the confidence of international partners, who closely monitor such milestones.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/08/27/guddiga-doorashooyinka-oo-shaaciyay-degmooyinka-doorashooyinka-hirshabeelle/",
